      "name": null,
      "problem": "The point $(1,2)$ is stretched with invariant $y$-axis and stretch factor $-3,$ and then stretched with invariant $x$-axis and stretch factor $2.$ What is the resulting point?",
      "worked_solution": "Let's apply the given transformation.\n\n- A stretch of factor $-3$ and invariant $y$-axis can be represented by the function\n\n$$\n(x,y)↦(-3x,y).\n$$\n\n- A stretch of factor $2$ and invariant $x$-axis can be represented by the function\n\n$$\n(x,y)↦(x,2y).\n$$\n\nTherefore, the combination of the stretches is given by\n\n$$\n(x,y)↦(-3x,2y).\n$$\n\nApplying the combined stretch to our point, we obtain\n\n$$\n(1,2)↦(-3\\cdot 1,\\,2\\cdot 2)=(-3,4).\n$$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14275005/assets/9379cdda26ca60ad8e9bf9486bbdba9d547361517b057944d154476f1828c526.png)",
